  "steps": [
    "Put the beef mince, breadcrumbs, egg, grated onion, minced garlic, chopped parsley, salt and black pepper into a bowl. Mix gently until just combined, then shape into about 16 meatballs.",
    "Heat 1 tablespoon of the olive oil in a large frying pan over medium heat. Brown the meatballs in batches for 4 to 5 minutes, turning them so they colour all over. Transfer to a plate.",
    "Add the remaining olive oil to the pan and cook the sliced onion for 5 minutes until soft. Add the sliced garlic and paprika and cook for 30 seconds until fragrant.",
    "Stir in the canned tomatoes, tomato paste, water, sugar, salt and black pepper. Bring to a gentle simmer.",
    "Return the meatballs to the pan, cover loosely and cook for 15 to 18 minutes, turning once, until the meatballs are cooked through and the sauce has thickened.",
    "Taste and adjust the seasoning. Scatter over the remaining parsley and serve hot."
  ],
